Z||000000||reddog||10-23-2001||05:35 AM||||Hello I just took my GT on a trip to a near by city. When I got on the interstate and got over 65mph I noticed a really bad vibration/ shaking that seemed to start in the steering and would work its way back to the rear. it would do this in a wave like effect constantly. (Front to Back) Occassionally in would all smooth out for a second in a slight curve to the left or right. I did a search just now and found that GTmike had the same problem but there was no post or reply that stated what it took to fix the problem.<BR>By the way I just put new 17" wheels and tires on my car Nankang 215/45/17 & 235/45/17 and have had them balanced twice so far! Someone please HELP!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picture_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-23-2001||07:34 AM||||Tires out of round, lug nuts not tight, bearings going, shocks/struts, tie rods, ball joints, alignment.<P>With the new larger wheels there may be some car geometry that has been changed and not been compensated for.<P>If you still have the old stock wheels, put them back on and see if the problem still exists.  That would narrow the focus, between wheels and suspension.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||10-23-2001||11:13 AM||||Have the tires balanced or replaced.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
